## Entry 5 — Detailed Quality Review of Chapter 1

**Date:** 22 October 2026
**Activity:** Reviewing Chapter 1 — Introduction to Artificial Intelligence
**Related Document:** `reviews/detailed-reviews/QR-001.md`
**AI Use:** Yes — ChatGPT

### What I Did

I reviewed Chapter 1, which was prepared by Jonathan Sugianto.

My responsibility was to evaluate the chapter rather than rewrite it for the author.

I compared the chapter with the module outline and examined whether the explanations were accurate and understandable for beginner students.

### Main Findings

The review identified several issues.

One concern involved the explanation of machine learning and supervised learning.

Another involved the interpretation of spam-filtering scores.

I also examined the comparison between rule-based and learning-based systems because this was specifically required by the module outline.

In addition to the technical content, the review considered image attribution and Markdown-related presentation issues.

### Evidence — Selected Findings

| Finding               | Explanation                                                                                      |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Supervised learning   | The chapter needed to distinguish supervised learning from machine learning in general           |
| Spam-filtering scores | A score should not automatically be described as a calibrated probability                        |
| Rule-based comparison | The example needed to clearly show the difference between fixed rules and learning from examples |
| Images and references | Attribution and presentation needed checking                                                     |
| Markdown navigation   | Table-of-contents links needed verification                                                      |

**Related file:** `reviews/detailed-reviews/QR-001.md`

### AI Use

**Tool:** ChatGPT

I used ChatGPT to help analyze the chapter and organize possible quality issues.

The AI-assisted discussion helped identify technical points that required closer attention.

I then compared those points with the actual chapter content and the module outline.

I did not consider every AI suggestion equally important. I focused on findings that affected accuracy, clarity, or assignment requirements.

### What I Learned

This review helped me understand that a chapter can sound reasonable but still contain explanations that are too broad or potentially misleading.

I also learned that useful review feedback should explain why a problem matters.

### Outcome

I prepared the Chapter 1 detailed review findings under QR-001.

