# Overall Reflection

My main contribution during Stage 1 was working as the Quality Lead for our AI Overview project.

This involved more than checking the accuracy of the Study Guide.

I also worked on the GitHub repository, created branches, prepared review standards, organized the Review Register, wrote detailed review findings, checked revisions, and organized the team AI Use Log.

One of my biggest challenges was understanding how to document quality review work properly.

At first, I was more focused on finding problems in the content.

As I continued working, I realized that identifying an issue was only one part of the process. I also needed to explain why the issue mattered, connect it to the learning objectives, and record it in a way that other members could understand.

Reviewing Chapters 1 and 2 helped me improve my understanding of AI concepts.

For Chapter 1, I learned more about the differences between rule-based systems, machine learning, and supervised learning.

For Chapter 2, I became more familiar with the different classifications of AI and the importance of covering all required topics.

I also gained experience using Markdown and GitHub for team documentation.

Creating branches and organizing review files helped me understand how a shared repository can support collaboration.

Another important part of my work was organizing the team's AI Use Log.

This made me think more carefully about the difference between using AI as a supporting tool and relying on AI to complete an assignment.

Overall, Stage 1 helped me become more confident in organizing project work and evaluating educational content.

I still want to improve my technical understanding and my ability to review material independently, but I now have a clearer understanding of what a Quality Lead should do.

